From b11cdce43526a4186b4380c0e6208eec78fdd16b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dallas Delaney <dadelan@microsoft.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 23:32:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] erofs: gate dm-verity on signed metadata

Use dm-verity only when a layer carries validated signature and root-hash metadata, while preserving plain EROFS for unsigned layers in optional mode. Persist materialization policy across ChainID reuse, validate concrete differ/snapshotter capability pairs, and retain upgrade compatibility for legacy unsigned snapshots.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

Copilot-Session: 925784b1-44a7-4d56-b04f-e527d2e0879f
